my_str2 = "world"
str_plus_str= my_str1 + ' ' + my_str2
print(str_plusstr)  #Hello World 

 Repeating strings 
sound = 'ha'
repeated_sound= sound*3
print(repeated_sound) #hahaha

NOTE: Concatenation only works with strings, otherwise you'll get TypeError.

We can convert numbers to strings using str()
name = 'john Doe'
age = 26 
name_and_age = name + str(age)
print(name_and_age) #John Doe26 

Augmented assignment operator for concatenation and assignment in one step (+=)
name = 'John Doe'
age = 26
name_and_age = name
name_and_age += str(age) 
print (name_and_age)  # John Doe26

String interpolation
inseting variables and expresions into a string
using f stings (formatted string literals) and curly brackets{}
name = 'john Doe'
age = 26 
name_and_age = f'My name is {name} and i am {age} years old'
print(name_and_age) # My name i sJon Doe and i am 26 years old 

NOTE: you dont need to use str() on non-string values 


